  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "From low to high the beast ladder runs Hundred Beast King, Thousand Beast King, myriad beast king, then beast emperor. Three groups of myriad foxes in Hu Immortal blessed land mean three myriad beast kings; that land has not yet produced a beast emperor.",
      "chapters": [
        409
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_hundred_beast_king",
        "sys_thousand_beast_king",
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ba Huang and Ying Ming of the three kings inheritance are beast emperors with battle strength that can match rank five Gu Masters. The text also calls them dog emperors.",
      "chapters": [
        409
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ba_huang",
        "char_ying_ming",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya’s rank seven beast enslavement Gu can subdue wild beasts including mutated beasts, myriad beast emperor, desolate beasts, and ancient desolate beasts.",
      "chapters": [
        463
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_lang_ya_sect",
        "gu_beast_enslavement_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Beast groups are classified as ordinary beasts, hundred beast king, thousand beast king, and myriad beast king, with beast emperor above myriad beast king. Wild Gu at rank five reside in a beast emperor’s body; such an emperor has rank five battle strength and can control myriad beast kings. Gu Immortals rarely sell beast emperors, because they reflect a blessed land’s strength, though wounded examples such as an old night wolf beast emperor still appear briefly in treasure yellow heaven and are bought quickly.",
      "chapters": [
        491
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
